{
    desc => q{Setting a mark overwrites the previous value at that mark},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/mark_overwrite`

Setting the same mark twice replaces the old position with the new one. **ma** on line 1, then **ma** on line 4 — jumping back with `` `a `` goes to line 4.

**Keys:** `ma` then `jjj` then `ma` then `` `a ``

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0

**after_first_mark.png**
- Mark 'a' set at line 1, col 0

**after_move_down.png**
- Cursor at line 4, col 0

**after_overwrite_mark.png**
- Mark 'a' overwritten at line 4, col 0

**after_jump_overwritten.png**
- Cursor at line 4, col 0 (the overwritten position, not line 1)
- Old mark position (line 1) discarded
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('ma');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_first_mark');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('jjj');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_down');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('ma');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_overwrite_mark');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('`a');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_jump_overwritten');
    },
}
__DATA__
line one
line two
line three
line four
line five
